SWEET ACM: a context store so iOS 26 can set a passcode, and selector 15 resolving it (2323)

iOS 26 never hands keybag the new passcode. profiled puts it in an ACM context
(ACMContextCreate, ACMContextSetData type 7), exports the context's 16-byte id
(ACMContextGetExternalForm) and calls MKBKeyBagChangeSystemSecretWithACM with the
ids. MobileKeyBag sets 0x4 in the params word, keybagd passes the ids and the word
through untouched, and libaks puts them in selector 15's scalars 3/4, 5/6 and 11.
With no AppleCredentialManager in the kernel the very first ACM call fails with -5,
so no code can be set (plans/passcode/TURNON-ast228.md, "The second wall"). If the
ids did reach 2321 it would hash the id, and the lock screen, which sends the code
in the clear, could never unlock it.

- AppleCredentialManager, an IOResources service, exists only with sweetacm=1. Off,
  start() fails and every ACMLib call answers -5 exactly as before.
- AppleCredentialManagerUserClient (the class name the sandbox profiles allow) opens
  only for com.apple.private.applecredentialmanager.allow, is pinned to the task
  that opened it, and takes ACMLib's 'DRCS' commands inband on selector 0:
  create (0x24, 0x34, 0x01), set data (0x28), export (0x13), import (0x25, 0x12),
  get data (0x29) and delete (0x02). Everything else answers -5.
- The store (bsd/dev/SweetACMStore.c, compiled unchanged by the Mac host test):
  random 16-byte ids, type 7 only, 1..128 bytes, 16 contexts per connection and 64
  in all, fixed storage. Only the creating connection may set, read, export or
  delete a context; another may import an exported id and learns nothing else.
  Data is wiped on replace, delete, close and free. Nothing is logged.
- Selector 15: with 0x4 in scalar 11 the codes are 16-byte ids, resolved through
  the store to the bytes profiled stored (exported contexts that hold data only).
  Anything that does not resolve is refused before the core runs, so it is neither
  hashed nor counted, and an id never becomes an empty, clearing code. Without the
  bit nothing changes. Every 2321 check is unchanged.

Not done: selector 5 (set_system) and the change epilogue with ACM ids. keybagd's
two-phase change still fails after selector 15 on this kernel; see the audit brief.

Needs 2321 and 2322. Security code: plans/passcode/audit-brief-acm.md is the
audit brief, and no image should boot until that audit is a GO.

Check: python3 -I plans/passcode/tools/check-acm.py XNU_DIR (31 checks, 20 negative controls)
       python3 -I plans/passcode/tools/check-lock.py XNU_DIR (2321/2322, unchanged: 56 checks)
Apply: git apply -p1 in the kernel tree, after 2321 and 2322.
